commit 700f4d4558c2ae07f24fc796bc7145185fce6cdd
Author: Burak Emre Kabakcı <emrekabakci@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 04:49:21 2026 +0100

    fix(entities): stop a numeric schema enum from crashing the entity page (#828)

    A JSON Schema `enum` is not required to hold strings, but `formatLabel` and
    `humanizeToken` both took `string` and called `.split` / `.replace` directly.
    A numeric enum such as `vat_rate: [0, 1, 10, 20]` therefore threw
    "key.split is not a function" and took down the whole entity detail page
    rather than degrading a single field.

    Both helpers now accept `unknown` and coerce, which fixes the class rather
    than the one call site.

    Also fixes a latent round-trip bug behind it: a Select only ever emits
    strings, so choosing a numeric enum value wrote "20" into metadata instead
    of 20 and would then fail validation on save. Options render as strings and
    convert back when the property is `number`/`integer`.

